  "details": "With Unity’s default array fields, you can drag objects onto the array’s header to add them as new elements.\n\nHowever, `Face Tracking Meshes` array field on VRCAvatarDescriptor does not support dropping Skinned Mesh Renderers to add Face Tracking Meshes.\n\nIt's a small UX issue, but users familiar with Unity expect this to work, so it's surprising when it doesn't.",
